{
  "_comment": "Panel art for 'The Inkbound' episode 2. Fetched into the repo by .github/workflows/content-utils.yml, task `manhua-art-fetch` (which runs fetch-manhua-art.mjs on this file and commits the result) — the agent sandbox has no route to the generation CDN, a GitHub runner does. The `file` names are what data/manhua/inkbound-hsk2-ep02.json's panels[].art refer to; src/manhuaEpisodes.test.js fails if the two ever disagree.",
  "_style_comment": "All nineteen generated with the locked art direction in docs/STORY-BIBLE.md §6, model nano_banana_pro at 2k. Every panel featuring 小雨 or 小白 carried that character's model sheet from data/manhua/bible/ as a reference image, which is what keeps them the same person as episode 1. The 2/1 letterbox panels were generated at 21:9 and are cover-cropped by the reader. ⚠ Fourteen of the nineteen are SECOND takes: the first pass drew comic-page furniture the format cannot have — baked panel borders and white margins, empty caption boxes, an inset panel-within-a-panel, red seal stamps carrying invented glyphs, and (worst) pages covered in fake hanzi. Every prompt now carries an explicit full-bleed / no-frame / no-seal / no-invented-glyph block. See docs/STORY-BIBLE.md §6.",
